    belongs, including the paragraph on the name "Gutium" being extended by
    the Assyrians and Babylonians and surviving as far as Gubaru, "governor of
    Gutium" [[ ^4 ]][[ ^5 ]]. Several sentences in the source carry no
    footnote at all — the subduing of Uruk in about 2147~2050 BCE, Gudea and
